  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "open",
      "start": 0,
      "seconds": 18.333333333333332,
      "frames": 550,
      "lines": [
        {
          "file": "audio/open-1.wav",
          "text": "On a perpetuals exchange, a liquidation is never just one liquidation.",
          "start": 1.6,
          "seconds": 4.839979166666667
        },
        {
          "file": "audio/open-2.wav",
          "text": "It sells into the book, the bids thin out, the mark slips, and the next position falls.",
          "start": 6.7599791666666675,
          "seconds": 5.6399791666666665
        },
        {
          "file": "audio/open-3.wav",
          "text": "Domino lets you watch that chain reaction on Strike Finance, before it happens.",
          "start": 12.719958333333334,
          "seconds": 4.799979166666667
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "engine",
      "start": 18.333333333333332,
      "seconds": 26.8,
      "frames": 804,
      "lines": [
        {
          "file": "audio/engine-1.wav",
          "text": "Strike liquidates carefully.",
          "start": 0.4,
          "seconds": 2.0399791666666665
        },
        {
          "file": "audio/engine-2.wav",
          "text": "A position is closed in up to five staged IOC orders, each bounded by a neutral price that protects the trader.",
          "start": 2.759979166666666,
          "seconds": 6.6399791666666665
        },
        {
          "file": "audio/engine-3.wav",
          "text": "Whatever the book can't absorb goes to the SLP vault, and when that's full, profitable traders on the other side are auto-deleveraged.",
          "start": 9.719958333333333,
          "seconds": 7.359979166666666
        },
        {
          "file": "audio/engine-4.wav",
          "text": "Domino ports every one of those rules to TypeScript, and replays them second by second, against every live position and the real order books.",
          "start": 17.3999375,
          "seconds": 8.799979166666667
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "proof",
      "start": 45.13333333333333,
      "seconds": 12.433333333333334,
      "frames": 373,
      "lines": [
        {
          "file": "audio/proof-1.wav",
          "text": "Before simulating anything, it checks itself.",
          "start": 0.3,
          "seconds": 2.7999791666666667
        },
        {
          "file": "audio/proof-2.wav",
          "text": "From public API data alone, Domino reproduces all 472 liquidation prices Strike serves. Exactly.",
          "start": 3.4199791666666663,
          "seconds": 7.999979166666667
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "radar",
      "start": 57.56666666666666,
      "seconds": 24.833333333333332,
      "frames": 745,
      "lines": [
        {
          "file": "audio/radar-1.wav",
          "text": "The Risk Radar runs twenty full cascade replays and draws the exchange's stress curve.",
          "start": 0.5,
          "seconds": 5.359979166666666
        },
        {
          "file": "audio/radar-2.wav",
          "text": "In a 20% crash led by Bitcoin, 94 accounts get hit: $470k clears through the order book, and $132k lands on the SLP.",
          "start": 6.179979166666667,
          "seconds": 11.399979166666666
        },
        {
          "file": "audio/radar-3.wav",
          "text": "Below it, every market: where its next liquidation sits, and how much bid liquidity stands in front of it.",
          "start": 17.899958333333334,
          "seconds": 6.119979166666667
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lab",
      "start": 82.39999999999999,
      "seconds": 21.4,
      "frames": 642,
      "lines": [
        {
          "file": "audio/lab-1.wav",
          "text": "Click the curve, and the Cascade Lab plays that crash back, one mark-price batch at a time.",
          "start": 0.4,
          "seconds": 6.199979166666667
        },
        {
          "file": "audio/lab-2.wav",
          "text": "Above the axis, liquidation IOCs eat the resting bids. Below it, positions turn red as the cascade reaches them.",
          "start": 6.919979166666668,
          "seconds": 7.5999791666666665
        },
        {
          "file": "audio/lab-3.wav",
          "text": "And every IOC, SLP transfer and ADL fill lands in the log, in engine order.",
          "start": 14.839958333333335,
          "seconds": 5.759979166666667
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "catch",
      "start": 103.79999999999998,
      "seconds": 21,
      "frames": 630,
      "lines": [
        {
          "file": "audio/catch-1.wav",
          "text": "So where is liquidity missing?",
          "start": 0.4,
          "seconds": 1.9999791666666666
        },
        {
          "file": "audio/catch-2.wav",
          "text": "Domino finds the IOC limits the book could not fill, and prices post-only bids right there.",
          "start": 2.7199791666666666,
          "seconds": 6.239979166666667
        },
        {
          "file": "audio/catch-3.wav",
          "text": "If ADA crashes 30%, $10k of bids moves almost $9k of liquidations off the SLP and back onto the order book.",
          "start": 9.279958333333333,
          "seconds": 10.719979166666667
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "xray",
      "start": 124.79999999999998,
      "seconds": 12.566666666666666,
      "frames": 377,
      "lines": [
        {
          "file": "audio/xray-1.wav",
          "text": "Paste any wallet into Position X-Ray.",
          "start": 0.4,
          "seconds": 2.6399791666666665
        },
        {
          "file": "audio/xray-2.wav",
          "text": "This $103k oil long is 9.5% from liquidation. To survive a 15% cascade, it needs to cut 35%.",
          "start": 3.3599791666666663,
          "seconds": 8.599979166666667
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "guardian",
      "start": 137.36666666666665,
      "seconds": 9.666666666666666,
      "frames": 290,
      "lines": [
        {
          "file": "audio/guardian-1.wav",
          "text": "Guardian turns that into a bot.",
          "start": 0.3,
          "seconds": 2.0799791666666665
        },
        {
          "file": "audio/guardian-2.wav",
